# Log Detective 🔐

A Python-based cybersecurity learning project focused on analyzing synthetic authentication logs and detecting suspicious login activity.

## Project Status

🚧 In development — initial repository setup.

## Objective

The goal of Log Detective is to build a command-line tool that can identify potentially suspicious authentication patterns in log files.

This project is designed to explore Python programming, log analysis, time-based detection rules, and defensive cybersecurity concepts.

## Planned Features

- Parse synthetic authentication logs.
- Identify failed login attempts.
- Group authentication events by source IP address.
- Detect repeated failures within a configurable time window.
- Generate readable security alerts.
- Export analysis reports.
- Validate detection logic using automated tests.

## Technologies

- Python 3.13
- Python standard library
- pytest (planned for automated testing)
- Git and GitHub

## Planned Project Structure

```text
src/log_detective/   Python source code
data/                Synthetic sample logs
tests/               Automated tests
reports/             Generated reports
```

## Getting Started

Installation and usage instructions will be added once the first working version is available.

## Security and Ethics

This project uses synthetic authentication logs for educational purposes. It is intended for defensive security learning and does not perform attacks against real systems.

